  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name then family name, often with a middle name. Many surnames are old -sen patronymics (Hansen, Johansen) and many others are farm names (Berg, Haugen, Bakken, Dahl). People talk in their own dialect and write Bokmål or Nynorsk. First names and 'du' are used with everyone, including bosses. Sámi names come from the north, with surnames like Sara, Eira or Hætta. Norwegians with Pakistani, Somali, Polish or Middle Eastern roots usually keep family names from their parents' language; Polish women's surnames end in -ska.",
